// Title: File Explorer Folder Opened Using Explorer Folder Shortcut Via Shell
// Sigma ID: c3d76afc-93df-461e-8e67-9b2bad3f2ac4
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: @Kostastsale
// Date: 2022-12-22 | Modified: 2024-08-23
// ATT&CK: discovery, T1135
// Description: Detects the initial execution of "cmd.exe" which spawns "explorer.exe" with the appropriate
//   command line arguments for opening the "My Computer" folder.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://ss64.com/nt/shell.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_explorer_folder_shortcut_via_shell_binary.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\cmd.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\powershell.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\pwsh.exe") and FolderPath endswith "\\explorer.exe" and ProcessCommandLine contains "shell:mycomputerfolder"
